n to the","+ * previously installed handler instead of being captured. That handler is","+ * called directly, so it also receives error levels it was not registered for.","+ *","+ * @internal","+ */","+final class ErrorScope","+{","+    private ?string $error = null;","+","+    /**","+     * @template T","+     *","+     * @param callable(): T $operation","+     *","+     * @return T","+     */","+    public function run(callable $operation)","+    {","+        $previous = null;","+        $previous = set_error_handler(static function (int $errno, string $errstr, ...$rest) use (&$previous): bool {","+            foreach (debug_backtrace(\\DEBUG_BACKTRACE_PROVIDE_OBJECT | \\DEBUG_BACKTRACE_IGNORE_ARGS) as $frame) {","+                $scope = $frame['object'] ?? null;","+                if ($scope instanceof self) {","+                    $scope->error = $errstr;","+","+                    return true;","+                }","+            }","+","+            return $previous !== null && $previous($errno, $errstr, ...$rest) !== false;","+        });","+","+        try {","+            return $operation();","+        } finally {","+            restore_error_handler();","+        }","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * Returns the message of the last error captured, if any.","+     */","+    public function getError(): ?string","+    {","+        return $this->error;","+    }","+}"],"additions":58,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Utils.php","lines":["@@ -781,26 +781,26 @@ public static function streamFor($resource = '', array $options = []): StreamInt","     public static function tryFopen(string $filename, string $mode)","     {","         $ex = null;","-        set_error_handler(static function (int $errno, string $errstr) use ($filename, $mode, &$ex): bool {","-            $ex = new \\RuntimeException(sprintf('Unable to open %s using mode %s: %s', DiagnosticValue::escape($filename), DiagnosticValue::escape($mode), DiagnosticValue::escape($errstr)));","+        $scope = new ErrorScope();","+        $handle = $scope->run(static function () use ($filename, $mode, &$ex) {","+            try {","+                return fopen($filename, $mode);","+            } catch (\\Throwable $e) {","+                $ex = new \\RuntimeException(sprintf('Unable to open %s using mode %s: %s', DiagnosticValue::escape($filename), DiagnosticValue::escape($mode), $e->getMessage()), 0, $e);","+            }"," ","-            return true;","+            return false;","         });"," ","-        try {","-            /** @var resource $handle */","-            $handle = fopen($filename, $mode);","-        } catch (\\Throwable $e) {","-            $ex = new \\RuntimeException(sprintf('Unable to open %s using mode %s: %s', DiagnosticValue::escape($filename), DiagnosticValue::escape($mode), $e->getMessage()), 0, $e);","+        if ($ex === null && $scope->getError() !== null) {","+            $ex = new \\RuntimeException(sprintf('Unable to open %s using mode %s: %s', DiagnosticValue::escape($filename), DiagnosticValue::escape($mode), DiagnosticValue::escape($scope->getError())));","         }"," ","-        restore_error_handler();","-","         if ($ex) {","-            /** @var \\RuntimeException $ex */","             throw $ex;","         }"," ","+        /** @var resource $handle */","         return $handle;","     }"," ","@@ -824,38 +824,42 @@ public static function tryFopen(string $filename, string $mode)","     public static function tryGetContents($stream): string","     {","         $ex = null;","-        set_error_handler(static function (int $errno, string $errstr) use (&$ex): bool {","-            $ex = new \\RuntimeException(sprintf('Unable to read stream contents: %s', DiagnosticValue::escape($errstr)));","-","-            return true;","-        });","-","-        try {","-            /** @var string|false $contents */","-            $contents = stream_get_contents($stream);","+        $scope = new ErrorScope();","+        $contents = $scope->run(static function () use ($stream, &$ex) {","+            try {","+                /** @var string|false $contents */","+                $contents = stream_get_contents($stream);","+","+                if ($contents === false) {","+                    $ex = StreamTimeout::isResourceReadTimedOut($stream)","+                        ? new TimeoutException('Unable to read stream contents: timed out')","+                        : new \\RuntimeException('Unable to read stream contents');","+                } elseif (StreamTimeout::isResourceReadTimedOut($stream)) {","+                    $ex = new TimeoutException('Unable to read stream contents: timed out');","+                }"," ","-            if ($contents === false) {","+                return $contents;","+            } catch (TimeoutException $e) {","+                $ex = $e;","+            } catch (\\Throwable $e) {","                 $ex = StreamTimeout::isResourceReadTimedOut($stream)","-                    ? new TimeoutException('Unable to read stream contents: timed out')","-                    : new \\RuntimeException('Unable to read stream contents');","-            } elseif (StreamTimeout::isResourceReadTimedOut($stream)) {","-                $ex = new TimeoutException('Unable to read stream contents: timed out');","+                    ? new TimeoutException('Unable to read stream contents: timed out', 0, $e)","+                    : new \\RuntimeException(sprintf('Unable to read stream contents: %s', $e->getMessage()), 0, $e);","             }","-        } catch (TimeoutException $e) {","-            $ex = $e;","-        } catch (\\Throwable $e) {","-            $ex = StreamTimeout::isResourceReadTimedOut($stream)","-                ? new TimeoutException('Unable to read stream contents: timed out', 0, $e)","-                : new \\RuntimeException(sprintf('Unable to read stream contents: %s', $e->getMessage()), 0, $e);","-        }"," ","-        restore_error_handler();","+            return false;","+        });","+","+        if ($ex === null && $scope->getError() !== null) {","+            $ex = new \\RuntimeException(sprintf('Unable to read stream contents: %s', DiagnosticValue::escape($scope->getError())));","+        }"," ","         if ($ex) {","             /** @var \\RuntimeException $ex */","             throw $ex;","         }"," ","+        /** @var string $contents */","         return $contents;","     }"," "],"additions":37,"deletions":33,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/ErrorScopeTest.php","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@","+<?php","+","+declare(strict_types=1);","+","+namespace GuzzleHttp\\Tests\\Psr7;","+","+use GuzzleHttp\\Psr7\\ErrorScope;","+use PHPUnit\\Framework\\TestCase;","+","+/**","+ * @covers \\GuzzleHttp\\Psr7\\ErrorScope","+ */","+class ErrorScopeTest extends TestCase","+{","+    public function testReturnsTheOperationResult(): void","+    {","+        $scope = new ErrorScope();","+","+        self::assertSame('result', $scope->run(static fn (): string => 'result'));","+        self::assertNull($scope->getError());","+    }","+","+    public function testCapturesErrorsRaisedBeneathTheCall(): void","+    {","+        $passedOn = [];","+        set_error_handler(static function (int $errno, string $errstr) use (&$passedOn): bool {","+            $passedOn[] = $errstr;","+","+            return true;","+        });","+","+        try {","+            $scope = new ErrorScope();","+            $scope->run(static function (): void {","+                trigger_error('first', E_USER_WARNING);","+                trigger_error('second', E_USER_NOTICE);","+            });","+        } finally {","+            restore_error_handler();","+        }","+","+        self::assertSame('second', $scope->getError());","+        self::assertSame([], $passedOn);","+    }","+","+    public function testRestoresTheErrorHandlerWhenTheOperationThrows(): void","+    {","+        $handler = static fn (): bool => true;","+        set_error_handler($handler);","+","+        try {","+            (new ErrorScope())->run(static function (): void {","+                throw new \\LogicException('failed');","+            });","+            self::fail('Expected the operation exception.');","+        } catch (\\LogicException $e) {","+            self::assertSame($handler, self::currentErrorHandler());","+        } finally {","+            restore_error_handler();","+        }","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * @requires PHP 8.1","+     */","+    public function testPassesOnErrorsRaisedOnAnotherCallStack(): void","+    {","+        $passedOn = [];","+        set_error_handler(static function (int $errno, string $errstr) use (&$passedOn): bool {","+            $passedOn[] = $errstr;","+","+            return true;","+        });","+","+        try {","+            $scope = new ErrorScope();","+            $fiber = new \\Fiber(static function () use ($scope): void {","+                $scope->run(static function (): void {","+                    \\Fiber::suspend();","+                });","+            });","+            $fiber->start();","+            trigger_error('unrelated', E_USER_WARNING);","+            $fiber->resume();","+        } finally {","+            restore_error_handler();","+        }","+","+        self::assertNull($scope->getError());","+        self::assertSame(['unrelated'], $passedOn);","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * @requires PHP 8.1","+     */","+    public function testCapturesErrorsForOverlappingScopesThatFinishOutOfOrder(): void","+    {","+        $first = new ErrorScope();","+        $second = new ErrorScope();","+        $start = static function (ErrorScope $scope, string $message): \\Fiber {","+            $fiber = new \\Fiber(static function () use ($scope, $message): void {","+                $scope->run(static function () use ($message): void {","+                    \\Fiber::suspend();","+                    trigger_error($message, E_USER_WARNING);","+                });","+            });","+            $fiber->start();","+","+            return $fiber;","+        };","+","+        $firstFiber = $start($first, 'first');","+        $secondFiber = $start($second, 'second');","+        $firstFiber->resume();","+        $secondFiber->resume();","+","+        self::assertSame('first', $first->getError());","+        self::assertSame('second', $second->getError());","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * @requires PHP 8.1","+     */","+    public function testRestoresTheErrorHandlerWhenItsFiberIsDestroyed(): void","+    {","+        $handler = static fn (): bool => true;","+        set_error_handler($handler);","+","+        try {","+            $fiber = new \\Fiber(static function (): void {","+                (new ErrorScope())->run(static function (): void {","+                    \\Fiber::suspend();","+                });","+            });","+            $fiber->start();","+            unset($fiber);","+","+            self::assertSame($handler, self::currentErrorHandler());","+        } finally {","+            restore_error_handler();","+        }","+    }","+","+    private static function currentErrorHandler(): ?callable","+    {","+        $handler = set_error_handler(null);","+        restore_error_handler();","+","+        return $handler;","+    }","+}"],"additions":151,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/UtilsTest.php","lines":["@@ -861,6 +861,42 @@ public function testGetsContentsThrowExceptionWhenCLosed(): void","         Psr7\\Utils::tryGetContents($r);","     }"," ","+    /**","+     * @requires PHP 8.1","+     */","+    public function testTryGetContentsPassesOnErrorsRaisedInOtherFibers(): void","+    {","+        $source = Psr7\\Utils::streamFor('contents');","+        $resource = Psr7\\StreamWrapper::getResource(FnStream::decorate($source, [","+            'read' => static function (int $length) use ($source): string {","+                \\Fiber::suspend();","+","+                return $source->read($length);","+            },","+        ]));","+        $passedOn = [];","+        set_error_handler(static function (int $errno, string $errstr) use (&$passedOn): bool {","+            $passedOn[] = $errstr;","+","+            return true;","+        });","+","+        try {","+            $fiber = new \\Fiber(static fn (): string => Psr7\\Utils::tryGetContents($resource));","+            $fiber->start();","+            trigger_error('unrelated', E_USER_WARNING);","+            while ($fiber->isSuspended()) {","+                $fiber->resume();","+            }","+        } finally {","+            restore_error_handler();","+            fclose($resource);","+        }","+","+        self::assertSame('contents', $fiber->getReturn());","+        self::assertSame(['unrelated'], $passedOn);","+    }","+","     public function testTryGetContentsThrowsTimeoutWhenReadReturnsFalseAndResourceTimedOut(): void","     {","         PhpStreamMock::$streamGetContentsReturnsFalse = true;",""],"additions":36,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":288,"deletions":51,"truncated":false,"file_count":6},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-13T17:04:50.179196+00:00"}